{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"199571e90ec1e7271dce85fd6ac644b86761156a64c93af7114db57106564fed","digest":{"component_or_area":"backtest planning corpus validation","key_entities":["scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py","PLANNING_CORPUS_SIZE","PLANNING_CORPUS_COMMITS","--check-planning-corpus","_resolve_bug_ticket","_ticket_type","PLANNING_CORPUS_BOUNDARY","ADJUDICATED_SUBSTANTIVE","REBAR_TRACKER_DIR"],"problem_keywords":["planning corpus","corpus size drift","pin","derivation","live ticket state","reclassification"],"propositions":["The corpus size assertion (PLANNING_CORPUS_SIZE = 113) is derived at runtime from live ticket state and drifts when tickets are reclassified or prefix resolution changes, causing the check to fail despite no code changes.","The planning analysis was a one-time hand-reviewed judgment over a fixed commit set that should be pinned by identity (exact SHAs), not by count, to be immune to tracker churn.","The check mode should iterate pinned SHAs directly instead of re-deriving membership from live ticket state, with per-row labels serving as best-effort artifact metadata only.","The module docstring claims the corpus is 'pinned and reproducible' but the code re-derives it at runtime, creating a documentation-implementation mismatch."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787893307571572001,"uuid":"995bee18-4523-4142-91bb-bc2da2fa38f6"}